{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "06503b9b8f124c8581d9b47e85e9098f",
    "m_Title": "READ ME FIRST: how this shader works",
    "m_Content": "WHAT IT IS\nAn unlit, transparent particle shader (NAMU / MasterShader). It builds two things: a colour (Base Color) and a transparency (Alpha). There is no lighting, so what you see is exactly what these two outputs say.\n\nONE TEXTURE, FOUR JOBS\n\"Main Tex\" is a packed texture. Each colour channel is a separate mask, and the graph samples the same texture several times, each time pulling out one channel:\n  R = the coloured shape\n  G = the dissolve / erosion pattern\n  B = where the secondary colour appears\n  A = the silhouette (opacity)\n\nDRIVEN BY THE PARTICLE SYSTEM\nMost of the \"look\" is not on the material, it comes per particle from the Particle System. In the Renderer module you must add Custom Vertex Streams in this order:\n  Color            -> Vertex Colour (RGB tint, A fade)\n  Custom1.xyzw     -> TEXCOORD1 (read as \"UV1\")\n  Custom2.xyzw     -> TEXCOORD2 (read as \"UV2\")\nMeaning of each value:\n  UV1.x = Intensity (brightness, can go above 1 for bloom)\n  UV1.y = Dissolve amount (0 = whole, 1 = gone)\n  UV1.z = Dissolve falloff (0 = hard burn line, higher = soft fade)\n  UV1.w = Soft particle fade distance\n  UV2.xyz = Secondary colour\n  UV2.w   = How much of the secondary colour to blend in\nSet these with Custom Data curves in the Particle System, so every particle can dissolve and glow on its own timing.\n\nMATERIAL PROPERTIES\n  Main Tex, OutlineColor, OutlineThickness,\n  DIstortionNoiseTex, DistortionScroll, DIstortion Str,\n  Use Soft Particle? (toggle)\n\nREADING ORDER (left to right)\n1. Distortion: wobbles the UVs, so every texture read after it is warped.\n2. Intensity / MainColor / Secondary Color: build the colour.\n3. Dissolve Sharpness / Dissolve / Dissolve Edge / Outline: eat the shape away and draw the rims.\n4. Alpha (+ SoftParticles): build the final transparency.\n5. Master Stack: Base Color and Alpha.\n\nRENDER SETTINGS\nSurface: Transparent, Alpha blending, Unlit, casts no shadows, renders both faces. Targets are URP and Built-In.",
    "m_TextSize": 1,
    "m_Theme": 4,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": -3338.0,
        "y": -1964.0,
        "width": 650.0,
        "height": 1200.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": ""
    }
}

