{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "4c2d9e9d9ac7483cb1738173227f39cf",
    "m_Title": "Dissolve: eats the shape away",
    "m_Content": "WHAT IT DOES\nMakes the particle erode away over its lifetime. This is the main dissolve. Its output is a 0 to 1 mask that multiplies into Alpha.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n  Pattern    = Main Tex G channel\n  Amount     = UV1.y (saturated to stay inside 0 to 1)\n  Falloff    = UV1.z, from the Dissolve Sharpness group\nThese three go into the \"Dissolve Function\" subgraph.\n\nINSIDE THE SUBGRAPH\nIt remaps the amount into the range (-Falloff, 1), then does Smoothstep(remapped, remapped + Falloff, pattern).\nThe remap is what guarantees the ends behave:\n  amount 0 -> mask is 1 everywhere (fully visible)\n  amount 1 -> mask is 0 everywhere (fully gone)\nFalloff sets how wide the grey transition band is.\n\nThe same subgraph is used again in Dissolve Edge, on a slightly shrunken pattern. That is how the rim is found.",
    "m_TextSize": 1,
    "m_Theme": 6,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": 226.0,
        "y": 622.0,
        "width": 1133.0,
        "height": 585.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": "565dc2ba97684f529ed113d6cb035b1c"
    }
}

