{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "826e9e9c6e414f6e98764de2b7ed759b",
    "m_Title": "SoftParticles: no hard cut against geometry",
    "m_Content": "WHAT IT DOES\nFades the particle out where it intersects solid geometry, so you do not see a hard slicing line where the sprite crosses the floor or a wall.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Scene Depth (Eye mode) = how far away the surface behind the particle is.\n2. Screen Position (Raw) .w = how far away the particle itself is.\n3. Depth minus particle depth = the gap between them.\n4. Divide by UV1.w (the fade distance from Custom1) and Saturate.\n   Result: 0 right at the surface, rising to 1 as the particle moves away from it.\n5. The Branch node checks the \"Use Soft Particle?\" toggle. On = use this fade, Off = pass 1 (no fade).\n\nREQUIREMENTS\nThe Depth Texture must be enabled in the URP Asset (or the camera), otherwise Scene Depth returns nothing useful and the particles can vanish or stop fading.\nUV1.w controls the softness distance: bigger value = longer, softer fade.",
    "m_TextSize": 1,
    "m_Theme": 7,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": 622.0,
        "y": 1915.0,
        "width": 1175.0,
        "height": 606.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": "8152903e983944758e5c763467c61365"
    }
}

