{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "b4a68756803c4ef8b5263252e8e04e41",
    "m_Title": "Alpha: the final transparency",
    "m_Content": "WHAT IT DOES\nMultiplies together everything that can make the particle fade, then clamps the result.\n\nTHE CHAIN\n  Main Tex A          (the silhouette)\n  x Dissolve mask     (from the Dissolve group)\n  x Soft particle fade(from the SoftParticles group)\n  x Vertex Colour A   (the particle Color over Lifetime alpha)\n  -> Saturate -> Alpha\n\nBecause they are multiplied, any single one of them going to 0 hides the particle. If your particles are invisible, check them in that order.\n\nSmall note: this group samples Main Tex again instead of reusing the earlier sample. Same texture, same UV, so the compiler normally folds them into one read. Harmless.",
    "m_TextSize": 1,
    "m_Theme": 3,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": 2180.0,
        "y": 1771.0,
        "width": 1188.0,
        "height": 536.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": "cd0f157220844cad99697343d1e92dca"
    }
}

