{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "fc780485b6de4f31968bf09d04c29fd3",
    "m_Title": "Distortion: the wobble",
    "m_Content": "WHAT IT DOES\nWarps the UVs so a flat sprite looks like moving liquid. Its output feeds the UV input of every Main Tex sample in the graph, so the whole particle wobbles together.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Time x DistortionScroll, added to UV0. That scrolls the noise texture. DistortionScroll X and Y set speed and direction.\n2. That scrolling UV samples DIstortionNoiseTex. Only the R channel is used.\n3. Noise R x (DIstortion Str x 0.1) becomes a small offset, copied into both X and Y of a Vector2.\n4. That offset is added to the clean UV0. The result is the distorted UV used everywhere else.\n\nKNOBS\n  DistortionScroll: how fast and in which direction the wobble travels.\n  DIstortion Str: how strong the warp is. It is scaled by 0.1 inside, so material values around 1 to 10 feel natural.\n\nTWO THINGS TO KNOW\nThe Sampler State is set to Clamp, so the pushed UVs do not repeat the sprite at the borders.\nThe extra Sample Texture 2D with nothing plugged into its Texture slot returns white (1), so multiplying by it changes nothing. It looks like a leftover hook for a second mask. Safe to ignore.",
    "m_TextSize": 1,
    "m_Theme": 2,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": -2642.0,
        "y": -250.0,
        "width": 1393.0,
        "height": 643.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": "29ede126813047ddbb22c80bb70b6e46"
    }
}

